            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0307" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Swansea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moorhead</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Swansea</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 3.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Affidavits five American negroes, crew British unarmed tank steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pinna</hi> bound from Newport News-Cardiff, cargo oil;
                    attacked by submarine, Bristol Channel near Milford Haven, 6.30, morning 12th,
                    warning shot sent across bows, steamer failed to stop, shell sent into steamer,
                    slightly injuring one American, no other casualties, steamer torpedoed after
                    crew disembarked in lifeboats; British patrol appeared, submarine submerged,
                    crew returned to steamer, submarine again appeared, torpedoed vessel while crew
                    on board, crew rescued by patrol boats.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moorhead</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
